{
  "_comment": [
    "Where every settable value sits on the 800x600 RCU screens, so a customer's",
    "centerline value can be printed in the same box the machine prints it in.",
    "",
    "Boxes are pixel coordinates on the original 800x600 screenshot. `norm` is the",
    "same box as fractions of width/height, so the map survives the images being",
    "resized or recompressed.",
    "",
    "`sample` is the value baked into the screenshot (a 14-head machine running",
    "POTATO CHIPS at 90.0g). It is what gets painted over, and it is useful for",
    "checking an overlay lands in the right place.",
    "",
    "Every field here was read off the actual screen, and the labels are the RCU's",
    "own wording. Sections cite the CCW R Operation Manual."
  ],
